# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in from Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API.
# Without these the app runs exactly as before: local-only progress, no accounts.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# RevenueCat Web Billing, from the RevenueCat dashboard → Project Settings → API keys → Web
# Billing. This one IS public, in the same way the Supabase anon key is: it identifies the project
# and grants nothing by itself. Leave it empty and the pricing page shows the fallback prices from
# src/billing/config.ts and declines to sell anything, which is the correct behaviour for a build
# with no payments configured.
VITE_REVENUECAT_PUBLIC_KEY=

# The tutor's Gemini key is NOT a variable in this file, and must never become one. Every
# VITE_-prefixed value is compiled into the bundle a learner downloads, so a key here is a key
# published to everyone who loads the page. It is an edge-function secret instead — set it in the
# Supabase dashboard under Edge Functions > Secrets, or:
#
#   supabase secrets set GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# A free key comes from Google AI Studio (aistudio.google.com/apikey). The free tier is rate
# limited per PROJECT, not per user, so every learner shares one allowance — which is what the
# per-user daily cap in the function exists to protect.
#
# EXCEPT for local development. The dev server has its own tutor route (see `tutorDevRoute` in
# vite.config.ts) which reads the key from .env.local through Vite's loadEnv — never through
# import.meta.env, so it stays in the Node process and out of the bundle. That means the tutor
# works locally with no Supabase deploy at all: add the line below to .env.local and restart dev.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY=...
#
# The name has no VITE_ prefix on purpose, and `src/shared/chat/secrets.test.ts` fails the build
# if anything under src/ ever reaches for it.

# RevenueCat's other two secrets are NOT variables in this file either, for the same reason as the
# Gemini key above, and `secrets.test.ts` fails the build if a `sk_` literal ever reaches src/:
#
#   supabase secrets set REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=...
#
# REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET is a string you invent. Set the SAME value in the RevenueCat dashboard
# under Integrations → Webhooks → Authorization header, and the function rejects anything else.
# Deploy the webhook with --no-verify-jwt: RevenueCat has no Supabase session to present, so the
# shared secret is what authenticates it.
#
#   supabase functions deploy revenuecat-webhook --no-verify-jwt
